## Reviewer points not applied
- a#6: do not append a Vietnamese reading to “TWD 1.57M”. A test pins that token.
- a#29: do not delete the difficulty row. The checker compares block structure, and ACCEPTED forbids dropping a table row.
- a#4 suggested label with no “10”: the checker counts that digit against the English source. “(Điều 10)” stays in the label; the wrong statute name does not.
- Translating the three institution lines by deleting the English names: the bio contract requires those names byte-identical, and it rejects Han in bios. Vietnamese sits in front of the English name.
- “會計師” on the lawyers-page description: the four-language gloss test requires vi, id, th, and fil to annotate the same characters. The gloss is on the role line, which is not that surface.
- 006: no sentence about the writer’s age was in the file. Only the flagged pivot was rewritten.
- 018 “1 phiếu” and “2/3”: no row asked to spell them out, and adding words would not remove the digits the checker already accepts.
